From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Skia] A whole-target repaint clears the target first

With damage used for compositing, a frame clears the target only when it
has a clear color, which outside async scrolling it does not; a frame that
repaints the whole target, as each frame of a scroll, then draws over the
old contents. A tiled GPU, as the Mali-450, reads those contents back into
its tile memory before it draws, a whole-target read for nothing: on the
Mali-450 a 1156x695 copy takes 4.2 ms without a clear and 2.4 ms with one.
Clear the target when it is redrawn whole.

---
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/skia/SkiaCompositingLayer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/skia/SkiaCompositingLayer.cpp
@@ -624,6 +624,10 @@
                 damageRegion->fillCanvasInDeviceSpace(canvas, clearPaint);
             } else
                 canvas.clear(*clearColor);
+        } else if (!damageRegion) {
+            // The whole target is redrawn, so its old contents are not needed: clearing it says so, and
+            // spares a tiled GPU reading them back into its tile memory before it draws.
+            canvas.clear(SK_ColorTRANSPARENT);
         }
 
         PaintContext context;
